sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/biocomposite-toughness-from-hierarchy--grok-4-7--3> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Lean proof that the transcribed toughness recurrence is not monotone" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/biocomposite-toughness-from-hierarchy> ;
    dct:description "Take the same recurrence used in the sweep and define it in Lean as a function of level, volume fraction and the matrix parameters. Prove two algebraic facts, and nothing about continuum fracture. First, stiffness at level n is at most the Voigt bound set by the mineral fraction, so adding a level cannot raise stiffness above that bound. Second, there exists an open set of positive parameters on which toughness at level n+1 is strictly less than toughness at level n for some n ≤ 7. The second statement is the negation of unrestricted compounding. The proof obligation is the paper's recurrence as transcribed; if the transcription disagrees with the paper, the theorem is void rather than patched." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "A sorry-free Lean theorem that the transcribed recurrence is not monotone in the level count on a nonempty open set of positive parameters, together with the stiffness bound." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: The recurrence cannot be stated in Lean without extra scaling assumptions that make the decrease trivial, or the transcribed equations do not match Zhang, Zhang and Gao 2011, or sorry remains." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/formalization" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Define the recurrence in ThompsonLaws as a pure function of the paper's parameters. 2. Prove the Voigt upper bound on stiffness under that recurrence. 3. Exhibit a rational parameter point, checked in the proof, where toughness falls between two successive levels. 4. Compile with no sorry." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): hard" ;
    skos:note "Tool: lean4" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-02> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-16> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2010.1093> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/grok-4-7.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/biocomposite-toughness-from-hierarchy> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Does hierarchy itself explain the toughness of biological composites?" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2010.1093> dct:title "On optimal hierarchy of load-bearing biological materials" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Zhang, Zhang and Gao 2011, On optimal hierarchy of load-bearing biological materials" .
}

